                <pb facs="0849" n="735" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg735"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.156/50: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Diplomatic Agent and
                        Consul General at Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Denning</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-11T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 11,
                                1922—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>22. Your November 9, 7 p.m.</p>
                <p>American Embassy Paris telegraphs that French Government attributes postponement
                    to financial reasons. Report local developments, and advise by cable of any
                    requests that you may receive looking to your joining in protest by Diplomatic
                    Corps against legality of concession.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
